{
  "working": "Identify products:\n(i) Zn + Cl₂ → ZnCl₂ (anhydrous). Zn²⁺ is d¹⁰, all electrons paired → diamagnetic.\n(ii) (NH₄)₂Cr₂O₇ → Cr₂O₃ (or CrO₃? typical decomposition gives Cr₂O₃). Cr³⁺ is d³, three unpaired electrons → paramagnetic.\n(iii) CH₄ + H₂O with Ni catalyst at 800–900 °C → methanol (CH₃OH) (typical product of methanol synthesis). Methanol has no unpaired electrons → diamagnetic.\n(iv) Cr³⁺ + excess NaOH → Cr(OH)₃ precipitate (or Cr(OH)₄⁻). Cr³⁺ remains d³, three unpaired electrons → paramagnetic.\nThus only reactions (i) and (iii) produce diamagnetic products. Total number = 2.",
